  "_comment_ConnectionStrings": [
    "Do NOT put a connection string here (#3) \u2014 this file is a template and its sibling",
    "appsettings.json is gitignored precisely because credentials leak that way.",
    "",
    "Local development \u2014 store it in .NET User Secrets, outside the repo tree:",
    "  dotnet user-secrets set \"ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection\" \"Server=tcp:<server>.database.windows.net,1433;Initial Catalog=<db>;User ID=<user>;Password=<pass>;Encrypt=True;\" --project CRM.API",
    "",
    "Azure \u2014 set the App Service connection string (or the application setting",
    "ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection). Better still, use a Managed Identity so there",
    "is no password to rotate at all."
  ],
  "Cors": {
    "AllowedOrigins": [
      "http://localhost:3000",
      "https://ssp-mock-up.vercel.app"
    ]
  },
  "Jwt": {
    "Key": "<32+ character signing secret \u2014 set via the Jwt__Key env var / Azure app setting, never commit a real value>",
    "Issuer": "ShinyStarCRM",
    "Audience": "ShinyStarCRM",
    "ExpiryMinutes": 480
  },
  "_comment_Mfa": [
    "EncryptionKey encrypts every enrolled user's TOTP secret at rest (AES-256-GCM). It must",
    "be base64 that decodes to EXACTLY 32 bytes: `openssl rand -base64 32`. Azure: set the",
    "application setting Mfa__EncryptionKey. Never commit a real value.",
    "",
    "THERE IS NO KEY ROTATION. Lose or change this key and every enrolled secret becomes",
    "undecryptable \u2014 the whole team falls back to recovery codes, then to admin resets. The",
    "stored blob carries a version byte so rotation could be added later; it has not been.",
    "",
    "The development placeholder is publicly known, so dev TOTP secrets are encrypted under a",
    "key anyone can read. That is fine for development and is exactly why a development",
    "database must never be promoted to production. Startup refuses the placeholder outside",
    "Development, the same way it refuses the Jwt:Key placeholder.",
    "",
    "Required=true is what makes MFA mandatory. Users who have not enrolled can still sign in,",
    "but every endpoint except enrollment, /api/auth/me and logout returns 403 with",
    "code=mfa_enrollment_required. Enforcement is server-side (MfaEnforcementFilter); the",
    "frontend redirect is only a convenience.",
    "",
    "BREAK-GLASS: an admin who loses both their authenticator and their recovery codes has no",
    "in-app way back, because the admin reset endpoint itself requires an Admin. The database",
    "owner clears it directly:",
    "  UPDATE Users SET MfaEnabled = 0, MfaSecret = NULL, LastTotpStep = 0, MfaEnabledAt = NULL",
    "    WHERE Email = '<address>';",
    "  DELETE FROM MfaRecoveryCodes WHERE UserId = (SELECT Id FROM Users WHERE Email = '<address>');",
    "The audit log records the consequences (the re-enrollment that follows) but NOT the DB",
    "edit itself \u2014 that is a real limitation, not an oversight."
  ],
  "Mfa": {
    "EncryptionKey": "<base64 of 32 random bytes \u2014 set via the Mfa__EncryptionKey env var / Azure app setting, never commit a real value>",
    "Required": true,
    "Issuer": "Shining Stars CRM"
  },
  "_comment_ForwardedHeaders": [
    "The frontend proxies every API call through its own origin, so the address this API",
    "sees is the proxy's, not the client's. List the proxy's outbound IP address(es) here to",
    "have X-Forwarded-For trusted from them \u2014 audit rows and the login rate limiter then see",
    "the real client. Azure: ForwardedHeaders__KnownProxies__0, __1, ...",
    "",
    "Empty is the safe default and is what production should keep until the API is network-",
    "restricted. This API is publicly reachable, so trusting X-Forwarded-For from ANY caller",
    "would let an attacker forge a new address per request and defeat the login rate limit",
    "entirely. Empty leaves the framework's loopback-only default, which is why local",
    "development already works: the Next.js dev server calls from 127.0.0.1.",
    "",
    "The complete fix is to restrict network access to this API (App Service access",
    "restrictions / private endpoint) so only the frontend can reach it; trusting the proxy",
    "is safe once nobody else can call in. Do that, then set KnownProxies to the frontend's",
    "egress address(es): until you do, every anonymous rate-limit budget (login, login-mfa)",
    "is shared by the whole organisation rather than being per-client, and staff can throttle",
    "each other while an attacker calling this API directly sits in a partition of their own.",
    "",
    "Not a secret \u2014 no startup guard, unlike Jwt:Key."
  ],
  "ForwardedHeaders": {
    "KnownProxies": []
  },
  "_comment_Database": [
    "MigrateOnStartup controls whether the app applies pending EF migrations when it boots.",
    "It defaults to TRUE in Development and FALSE everywhere else, so a production restart can",
    "never alter the schema on its own. Leave it unset in Azure App Service.",
    "",
    "Deploy order is therefore: run `dotnet ef database update --project CRM.Persistence",
    "--startup-project CRM.API` against the target database FIRST, then deploy the app. If you",
    "deploy first, the app refuses to start and names the pending migrations rather than",
    "half-migrating anything.",
    "",
    "Set Database__MigrateOnStartup=true only if you deliberately want boot-time migration back."
  ],
  "Database": {
    "MigrateOnStartup": false
  },
  "_comment_BlobStorage": [
    "Script PDFs live in Azure Blob Storage, not in the database. Leave both credentials empty",
    "and the API still starts \u2014 PDF uploads answer 503 'not configured' until one is set.",
    "",
    "AccountUrl (preferred): https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net. The API signs in with its",
    "App Service managed identity (DefaultAzureCredential), which needs the Storage Blob Data",
    "Contributor role on the storage account \u2014 nothing secret to store or rotate. Azure",
    "application setting: BlobStorage__AccountUrl.",
    "",
    "ConnectionString (alternative): the account's full connection string. It embeds the",
    "account key, so it is a secret \u2014 Azure app setting BlobStorage__ConnectionString or local",
    "user secrets only, never this file. Wins over AccountUrl when both are set, so a developer",
    "can point local runs at Azurite (UseDevelopmentStorage=true) without touching the deployed",
    "configuration.",
    "",
    "ContainerName defaults to crm-files and is created on first upload if it does not exist."
  ],
  "BlobStorage": {
    "AccountUrl": "<https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net \u2014 or leave empty and set BlobStorage__AccountUrl in Azure>",
    "ConnectionString": "",
    "ContainerName": "crm-files"
  }
}